Lab 8: Configuring sudo Rules
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Understand the concept of centralized sudo management in Identity Management (IdM)
Create and configure sudo rules using the ipa sudorule-add command
Assign sudo rules to specific users and groups within the IdM environment
Test and validate sudo access permissions with different user accounts
Troubleshoot common sudo rule configuration issues
Implement security best practices for sudo rule management
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with user and group management concepts
Knowledge of sudo fundamentals and basic usage
Understanding of Identity Management (IdM) server concepts
Completion of previous IdM labs covering user and group creation
Basic networking knowledge for client-server communication
